detailedAnswer:
When async operations do not depend on each other's results, running them in sequence creates unnecessary latency bottlenecks:

Sequential (Bad for independent requests):
for (const id of ids) {
  await fetchItem(id); // Wait 200ms * 10 = 2000ms
}

Parallel (Optimal):
const promises = ids.map(id => fetchItem(id));
const results = await Promise.all(promises); // Total: ~200ms total!

